-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;113,497&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:99.702%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.900%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.900%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.900%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.900%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.900%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="15" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2. LONG-TERM BORROWINGS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On December 8, 2025, the Company closed on a secured, revolving credit facility with outside lenders with a total capacity of $200 million. The loan bears interest at the daily Secured Overnight Financing Rate (SOFR) plus 1.375%.This facility has a maturity date of December 8, 2030.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;There have been no borrowings or repayments since the initial draw of $35.5M in December 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;3.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company entered into Corporate Support Services Agreements with subsidiaries of NextEra Energy, Inc. ("NextEra Energy") whereby the Companies pay a certain annual fee plus actual costs incurred in connection with administrative services performed under these agreements. Income is recorded directly as a reduction to the expenses. Amounts for these costs are included in accounts payable to associated companies or accounts receivable from associated companies. The Company has a payable to NextEra Energy for income taxes and various other items which are included in accounts payable to associated companies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;4.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;REGULATORY MATTERS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:10pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On May 13, 2024, the Company filed an application under sections 205 and 219 of the Federal Power Act to request incentive rate treatment for its investment in the North Gila- Imperial Valley #2 500 kV Line Project and the Imperial Valley &#8211; North of San Onofre Nuclear Generating Station ("SONGS") 500 kV Line and 500/230 kV Substation Project. For both projects, the Company requested authorization to include 100% of prudently incurred Construction Work in Progress in rate base, as well as to recover 100% of prudently incurred costs if the projects are abandoned for reasons beyond the Company&#8217;s control. FERC granted the Company's application in an order issued July 12, 2024. Since CWIP in rate base during the construction period is considered an acceleration of a return on the allowance for funds used during construction, the Company believes that prior to the Project going into service, CWIP in rate base is recorded as an Alternative Revenue Program (&#8220;ARP&#8221;),with any over or under collection reflected as a regulatory asset or liability. The income statement offset is reflected within revenue from regulatory mechanisms. Through September 30, 2026, the Company has recognized $3.0 million related to this program.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On August 19, 2024, the Company filed an application for authorization under section 204 of the Federal Power Act to make available long-term, secured debt securities in a principal amount not to exceed $200.0 million during a two year period to: fund construction of the Estrella Project, the North Gila Project, and the North of SONGS Project; to meet ongoing capital needs associated with the ownership and operation of the Suncrest Project; and to meet the Company&#8217;s ongoing working capital needs. FERC granted the Company&#8217;s application in an order issued on November 8, 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On January 10, 2025, the Company filed a Report of Securities Issued under the prior-effective section 204 authorization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On November 27, 2024, the Company filed, for informational purposes, its annual transmission formula rate informational filing, pursuant to Section 3 of the Company&#8217;s Formula Rate Implementation Protocols and Appendix F, Schedule 3 of the California Independent System Operator Corporation&#8217;s ("CAISO) Tariff.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On December 4, 2024, pursuant to section 205 of the Federal Power Act, the Company filed revisions to Appendix I of its Transmission Owner Tariff to reflect the annual update of its Transmission Revenue Balancing Account Adjustment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On January 29, 2025, FERC accepted the filing via delegated letter order, effective January 1, 2025, as requested.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On May 30, 2025, the Company filed in Docket No. ER25-2395-000, pursuant to section 205 of the Federal Power Act, an application seeking an increase on the base return on equity for the Company's projects (other than the Suncrest and Estrella Projects), which is stated in the Company's Formula Rate Template ("Template"), which is found in Appendix III of the Company's Transmission Owner Tariff ("TO Tariff"); add a prior period adjustment mechanism to the true-up mechanism in Attachment 5 of the Company's Template; and request authorization for any yet-to-be formed Company affiliate or subsidiary that is later formed to develop competitive transmission projects in the CAISO region to replicate the Company's TO Tariff through a future ministerial filing. The Company &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;requested an effective date of July 30, 2025, for the proposed revisions. On July 29, 2025, FERC accepted in part the proposed revisions, suspended them for five months to become effective November 20, 2025, subject to refund, and established hearing and settlement judge procedures. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On December 5, 2025, the California Department of Water Resources State Water Department (DWR) and the Northern California Power Agency (NCPA) filed a Preliminary Challenge to the Company's 2024 true-up expenses. Specifically, DWR and NCPA have challenged the variance between the Company's previous 2024 projection (filed in FERC Docket No. ER24-1298-000) and the 2024 Annual Update (filed at FERC in Docket No. ER26-946-000), costs related to the Suncrest project pursuant to its Approved Project Sponsor Agreement with CAISO, and Operations and Maintenance costs and Administrative and General expenses included in the 2024 Annual Update. The Company responded to the Preliminary Challenge, defending and supporting its 2024 Annual Update costs, on January 5, 2026. Discussions related to the Preliminary Challenge are ongoing. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;5.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;SUBSEQUENT EVENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company's management has evaluated the recognition and disclosure of subsequent events for its September 30, 2026 financial statements through November&#160;4, 2026, noting no additional disclosures are required.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
